  Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.
  Draft: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/selected-history-limits.tex>. This is
  a same-family application of the existing local convergence proofs, not an
  independent production of Fluent/FullPaths, the extended MailBox, the free
  Amplify horizon, or the funded nonlinear transitions.

  <section|Inspected declarations and meanings><label|inspected-declarations-and-meanings>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.MailBox>, <verbatim|.Inspected>,
    <verbatim|.haloB>, <verbatim|.settled>, <verbatim|.verdant>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Canvas/Mails.lean>: the true enlarged
    allowance is 64 times the path and loop budgets. MailBox also fixes Reel
    encodings, supplies strict row width via glyph, and supplies resumes on
    arbitrary attached enlarged inputs. Inspected records the chosen actual
    Bubble and Skies at each finite step. settled's backward induction
    chooses those paths and the exact scalar/stationary data together.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Artes.Counter>, <verbatim|.Alive.destiny>,
    <verbatim|.Alive.snips>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Artes/Gears.lean>:
    in addition to MailBox, Counter retains Suffices, all-period sworn data,
    LocalRatio and a nonempty color index. These are not inferred from the
    name of an input. The existing background-path convergence proof consumes
    their mathematical content.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Artes.Roadie>, <verbatim|.author>,
    <verbatim|.cruising>, <verbatim|.bud>, <verbatim|.daylight>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Artes/Letters.lean>: author uses one
    selection of coefficients for each actual path. Its
    input/output/scalar/stationary equalities require m+1\<less\>N; adjacent
    coefficient identity requires m+2\<less\>N. The manuscript keeps a tail
    where all hold.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Artes.Cadre>, <verbatim|.supreme>,
    <verbatim|.yields>, <verbatim|.xerox>, <verbatim|.replayQ>,
    <verbatim|.history_copy>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Artes/Events.lean>:
    coefficient/scalar/ stationary convergence and a strict-width row bound.
    Every-subsequence uniqueness upgrades to the full sequence. Eventual
    copies preserve all these fields. No fresh compactness of completion
    balls is asserted.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Beacon.Calm>, <verbatim|.guides>,
    <verbatim|.harvest>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Regent/Receives.lean>:
    eventual Bounds, Drive on the common row dictionary, Reel.Price and
    common Flagship coefficient data; analytic chart readouts follow by
    normally convergent series.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Stationary.Artes.stillP>, <verbatim|.Rios>,
    <verbatim|.nativity>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Artes/Vogue.lean>: one
    width strictly above the paid width and below the row/three encoding
    widths; row and three atom differences all have arbitrarily small
    SumBudget. Row direction is separate in source; the manuscript sums the
    finite directions after shrinking epsilon. Local cove/trio proofs use
    summable channel weights, not arbitrary-walk counting. The exact sums are
    already proved in fixed-rung-convergence.tex.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.ThroughLaunch.Imperial>,
    <verbatim|.Perceived>, <verbatim|.changeP>, <verbatim|.sailsW>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Roll/Fiscal.lean>: strengthened public
    purchase, with Cadre and Amplify from the same MailBox and inspected
    construction. The terminal change preserves paths below the terminal
    scale, alpha everywhere, and stationary maps and full towers when
    m+1\<less\>N. It preserves beds for m\<less\>N and tower T for
    m\<less\>N. These exact identities are used by replayQ/history_copy.
    <verbatim|sailsV>/Torrent in MergeProof/Seaside.lean alone does not
    supply Cadre/Amplify.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Locrian>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Roll/Meridian.lean>: exactly the
    Cadre/Amplify pair.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Lark.Glide.Window.Banked>,
    <verbatim|.tickets>, <verbatim|.watts>, <verbatim|.pressing>,
    <verbatim|.palm>, <verbatim|.trader>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Glide/Kiosk.lean>; <verbatim|.allB>,
    <verbatim|Glide/Triumph.lean>; <verbatim|.accord>,
    <verbatim|Glide/Coincide.lean>: normalized coupling, completed activity
    and scalar-cost limits on the same path background. Existing
    coupled-background-convergence.tex supplies the proof, including finite
    telescoping and the same-cutoff fixed-script comparison. The scalar cost
    q is distinct from path alpha.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Campaign.Winter>,
    <verbatim|.offers>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Glide/Vac.lean>: path
    identity of actual competitors through rises.prices and bases; their Show
    representative has exactly the trail activities and embeds into
    Window.coats. These are the alignment identities used in the last
    subsection. No analyticity conclusion from Winter.analytic is claimed in
    this new unit.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Actual public binding><label|actual-public-binding>

  Directly inspected <verbatim|Lean/YM/Integration/NativeSelection/FundedCompanySelection.lean>:
  <verbatim|YM.Integration.NativeSelection.FundedCompanySelection.company>
  takes <verbatim|ThroughLaunch.Perceived>, calls companyK, and retains
  Cadre/Amplify on the exact Directed/Alloy returned while adding prediction
  and extra delay purchases. <verbatim|Integration/RG05Preconstruction/Expenses.lean>
  calls sailsW (not sailsV). Independent reviewer additionally identified
  <verbatim|RG05Joint.engageWithCustodyFactor>,
  <verbatim|Integration/RG05Preconstruction/PeriodConstruction.lean>, where
  the same receipts become Locrian literally as their pair. Parent checked
  the short binding at the construction of the Run and Campaign and the
  literal pair <verbatim|\<langle\>hP,he\<rangle\>> before integration; there
  is no license to substitute an independently chosen convergent run.

  <section|Existing proof reuse and remaining
  boundary><label|existing-proof-reuse-and-remaining-boundary>

  The analytic convergence proof is reused from background-path-convergence,
  fixed-rung-convergence, coupled-background-convergence,
  marked-kernel-convergence, local-source-stability and the finite-volume
  parameter comparison units. No literature substitution is introduced; the
  shared literature notes and those units already govern their analytic
  background. All same-history funded transition premises in
  parameter-comparison-suppliers remain. The one-step extended construction
  and convergent free horizon are explicit inputs; the annulus/FullPaths and
  free horizon producers must close them.

  <section|Commands and checks><label|commands-and-checks>

  Bounded rg/sed/cat reads of the named files and SHA256 of the draft. No
  Lean build, source changes, axiom replay or new literature claim.
  Independent review, integration, checker and PDF build pending.

